{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And he shall not be like Korah and his assembly.</b> From here our Sages of blessed memory proved that whoever maintains a dispute transgresses a negative commandment. And the explanation of the verse: ולא יהיה כקרח וכעדתו — he shall not be like Korah and his assembly — among those swallowed and those burned, but rather that he be stricken with tzara'at; this is 'as YHWH spoke by the hand of Moshe to him' — an allusion to those who contest the priesthood, that they are stricken with tzara'at just as Moshe was stricken with tzara'at in his hand, as it is written (Exodus 4:6): ״ויאמר ה׳ לו עוד הבא נא ידך בחיקך״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:33:24.917129470Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}